# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own key:
#     cp .env.example .env          (macOS/Linux/Git Bash)
#     copy .env.example .env        (Windows Command Prompt)
#
# .env is listed in .gitignore and is never committed. Only this example file,
# with the value left blank, is tracked in the repository.
#
# A key is OPTIONAL. The system has two generation backends (see generator.py):
#
#   - With a key: answers are generated by Groq (llama-3.3-70b-versatile).
#   - Without a key: answers are generated by a small local model
#     (Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct) that runs on CPU via transformers. It
#     downloads once (~1 GB) and needs no account and no network afterward.
#
# Both backends receive identical prompts and identical retrieved context, so
# grounding and source attribution behave the same either way. The local model
# writes blunter prose than the hosted one; that tradeoff is documented in the
# README.
#
# Get a free key (no credit card) at https://console.groq.com/keys
# Paste it after the '=' with no quotes and no spaces.

GROQ_API_KEY=
